## Desk guidance

For the shared parser, record the engineering fix and close its ticket as completed.
For the booking-v3 hint, record form retirement and close its ticket as not planned,
not completed. Do not equate retiring a feature with correcting its behavior.

Continue triaging reports by verified cause and affected path, not matching subjects
or browser-derived intake tags. For reports arriving after closure, check the deployed
parser version and whether the reporter still uses a retired form before merging.
Unknown tenants and conflicting evidence remain separate pending investigation.

The five desk-note reports R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 still
lack evidence for a distinct root cause. The export classifies them under parser
with a caveat; the engineering update does not independently diagnose each one.
Preserve the evidence if any symptom continues after the fix.

The published counts are deduplicated historical counts, not a live feed.
Refresh reports and tenant settings before making new claims about today's queue.

